{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"9c13d4f46772d15edb15e6acbcb0aa2c90116b9cd4cb48e9b35ac05ea910c3cf","digest":{"component_or_area":"identity key lifecycle and era-scoped authorship verification","key_entities":["KEY_ADD event type","KEY_REVOKE event type","src/rebar/reducer/_version.py","src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py","src/rebar/attest/authorship.py","src/rebar/_commands/identity.py","src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py","src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","process_key_event","verify_authorship_at_epoch","epoch_for_position","keyring","keyring_epoch","add_identity_key","revoke_identity_key"],"problem_keywords":["key rotation","cryptographic continuity","trust-on-first-use","authorship verification","key lifecycle","key revocation","era-scoped validity","signed rotation chain","identity key management"],"propositions":["KEY_ADD and KEY_REVOKE events establish a cryptographically signed rotation chain where each key operation after genesis must be authorized by a currently-valid key of the identity.","Key validity is scoped to an era determined by fold order (keyring_epoch), not by attacker-controllable event timestamps, preventing backdated key injection.","The genesis KEY_ADD for an identity is accepted without a signature (TOFU), but all subsequent key operations are refused unless accompanied by a valid authorship signature from a currently-valid key.","verify_authorship_at_epoch resolves a keyring and verifies authorship only against keys whose validity window contains the specified epoch, rejecting events signed with revoked keys.","Snapshot compaction correctly freezes and restores keyring state and keyring_epoch so that key validity epochs remain contiguous and consistent after snapshot replay."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timesta